.TH CSTRING_TO_UPPER 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cstring_to_upper \- convert the ASCII letters to uppercase in-place
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cstring.h>

void cstring_to_upper(cstr s);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function turns every ASCII lower-case letter of the string into upper
case, in place, and leaves every other byte as it is.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s   String to change
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Only the bytes 'a' to 'z' change, and the locale plays no part, so the
result is the same in every locale (a Turkish one included). A byte above
0x7F never changes, which keeps a UTF-8 string valid UTF-8
Asserts if s is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_to_lower (3)
